\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Projection role separates moment geometry and drift across Muon, MuonT, and WT-MLP-Lag.} \textbf  {(a)} 32-layer median diagonal anisotropy share ($\mathrm  {DiagAniso}$ in \cref  {eq:diag_aniso}) at step 2,500 (130M); its complement is the off-diagonal share. Expanded SwiGLU outputs (\texttt  {gate,up}) are predominantly diagonal across all three optimizers, whereas residual writers (\texttt  {o,down}) carry less than 1\% of anisotropy on the diagonal. \textbf  {(b)} 32-layer mean top-16 subspace drift from steps 2,250 to 2,500 (defined in \cref  {eq:subspace_drift}; $0$ denotes identical subspaces and $1$ orthogonal subspaces). \textbf  {(c)} Cumulative exact-eigendecomposition fallbacks across eight GPUs in the dense-output diagnostic run: dense outputs trigger 22.1 exact repairs per step versus 29 post-warmup fallbacks in total for dense inputs.}}{7}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
